  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Minthostachys mollis",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minthostachys_mollis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1252215221,
      "text": "Minthostachys mollis is a medicinal plant restricted to the South American Andes from Peru to Bolivia. It is the most variable and widely distributed species of the genus Minthostachys. Its common name muña comes from Quechua. Other local names include tipo, tipollo, poleo."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Minthostachys mollis",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minthostachys_mollis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 175711191,
      "text": "Minthostachys mollis, conocida comúnmente como muña, peperina, poleo de Quito, tifo o tipo es una especie de planta arbustiva leñosa, oriunda del Perú, Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Argentina y Venezuela."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Minthostachys mollis",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minthostachys_mollis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 239269413,
      "text": "Minthostachys mollis, aussi appelée muña, tipo, tipollo, poleo est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Lamiaceae. C'est une plante médicinale endémique des Andes que l'on trouve du Venezuela à la Bolivie. C'est l'espèce la plus largement répandue du genre Minthostachys."
    }
  },
